# sluicesync.com line-ending policy.
#
# The whole site is GENERATED: `node build.mjs` (and `demos/build-page.mjs`)
# writes every docs/*/index.html, docs/*/index.md, field-notes/*, the root
# landing page, screenshots/index.html, and llms.txt / llms-full.txt with LF
# line endings. The committed blobs are already uniformly LF. Under a
# contributor's `core.autocrlf=true`, checkout smudges some of those files to
# CRLF in the working tree, so the next `node build.mjs` rewrites them back to
# LF and they surface as phantom, line-ending-only diffs.
#
# Pinning the WORKING TREE to LF (eol=lf) makes the generator's output match
# what git expects on disk, so a rebuild produces no spurious changes. Because
# the index is already LF, this reconciles the working tree without rewriting
# any committed content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply text/eol filtering.
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
